//St. Martial Map Clues / Easter Eggs

//FIRST FLOOR


//Water Hose
"1_WaterHose" "Part of you thinks it would be kind of fun to smash the glass and pull the water hose out.  However, the part of you that enjoys breathing knows that Recluse wouldn't want you to be wasting precious time."

//Wall Painting
"1_Painting" "You don't get it."

//File Cabinet
"1_Cabinet" "It's locked.  Upon closer inspection, you notice that someone's tried to jimmy his way into this file cabinet - several times.  What's in there?"

//Television
"1_Television" "It's not turned on right now, but some of Marchand's staff were watching 'Face the Nation' on this television earlier."

//Magazines
"1_Magazines" "Under a few magazines, you spot the intriguing cover of Life magazine, dated March 8, 1963.  There is a haunting photograph of Jean Seberg on the cover."

//Bulletin Board
"1_OfficeBulletinBoard" "One of the notices on this bulletin board instructs all employees to be exceptionally vigilant while leaving and entering the building.  It looks like these employees are taking the safety of their boss very seriously."

//Papers on Floor
"1_FloorPapers" "Confidential documents left laying on the ground is probably not the wisest idea in a presidential building."

//Vending Machine
"1_VendingMachine" "The vending machine is filled with plenty of yummy candy treats such as Zagnut, Boston Baked Beans, 7-Up Bars, and everyone's new favorite:  Sweet Tarts!"

//Classroom Papers
"1_ClassroomPapers" "The papers on this desk outline a training program for firearm safety and employee participation."

//Boardroom Whiteboard
"1_BoardWhiteBoard" "While the white board appears blank, residue from a previous meeting outlines designated staff to cover security over all areas of the building, even the rooftop."

//Boardroom Cupboard
"1_BoardCupboard" "This cupboard is filled with Styrofoam cups, plastic sticks, Coffee-Mate, and...guns?"


//SECOND FLOOR

//Bookcase
"2_Bookcase" "As you sift through the various books, you notice the set of Encyclopedia Americana for 1963 by Grolier.  A few volumes are missing."

//Vending Machine
"2_VendingMachine" "Hey, who took all the Sweet Tarts!?"

//Boardroom Papers
"2_BoardroomPapers" "This stack of papers identifies the plan of action that the government servicemen intend to implement.  All this cloak and dagger stuff is making the staff nervous."

//Papers on Secretary Desk
"2_SecretaryPapers" "The secretary left a few scribbled notes on her desk.  One of the notes reveals the possible location of the elevator key to the Marchand suite.  How careless!"

//Locked Desk
"2_LockedDesk" "It's locked.  You could jimmy it open if you wanted, but you have a president to assassinate.  It's probably just stuffed with Brylcreem and shoe polish anyway."

//Water Fountain
"2_WaterFountain" "Mmmm water.  Refreshing!"

//Lobby Table Papers
"2_LobbyPapers" "A Post headline talks about how 200,000 civil rights demonstrators marched on Washington for jobs and freedom.  The pages are worn thin from wear."

//Locked Desk
"2_LockedDesk1" "This desk is unlocked.  As you open it, you find bid notices from various window washing companies.  It looks like the one on top was accepted."

//Plant in Hallway
"2_HallPlants" "Hey, this one is plastic!"

//Boardroom Cupboards
"2_BoardCupboards" "The cupboards are bare.  This is the Marchand building.  No one could cough up a few bucks for some snacks?"

//Painting
"2_Painting" "Wait a minute. This is a copy of the painting from downstairs!  How cheap!"

//Watercooler
"2_WaterCooler" "This is a particularly popular spot for staff to gather together and discuss the television programs they watched the night before."

//Bookcase
"2_Bookcase1" "This bookcase is filled with government procedural manuals.  Needless to say, even though they were printed in the last year, the volumes are covered in dust."

//Painting
"2_Painting2" "You don't get this one either.  What's with this style?  Why can't they put up a painting that actually looks like something?"


//THIRD FLOOR

//Vending Machine
"3_VendingMachine" "This machine is out of order.  It doesn't stop you from trying to reach inside and grab some candy, though."

//Clock
"3_Clock" "Wait a second.  The clock downstairs said 3 o'clock.  Has someone been messing with them?"

//Papers in Boardroom
"3_BoardroomPapers" "These papers are invitations for an office party in honor of someone named Fran Kubelik.  It looks like her birthday is coming up."

//Bookcase
"3_Bookcase" "This bookcase includes a large variety of government-issued publications.  However, judging from the copies of 'War of the Worlds', 'Orphans of the Sky', and 'Confessions of an Advertising Man', staff have no problem bringing in their personal collections, too."

//Papers on Table
"3_TablePapers" "Stuck in with the other publications is a copy of Life Magazine with a photograph of a very young Jackie Kennedy and her puppy on the cover."

//Weird Purple-lit Plant
"3_PurplePlant" "Is the lighting weird or is there something strange going on with this plant?  Was it an effect of the gas you piped in earlier?"

//Bulletin Board
"3_BulletinBoard" "This bulletin board is covered with reminders about staff meetings, upcoming company gatherings, and a 'watch list' for suspected villains in the area.  You scan for your name and come up empty.  Excellent.  The snake cave incident hasn't caught up with you...yet."

//File Cabinet
"3_FileCabinet" "As you pry open this file cabinet, you find staffing files on all of the employees under Marchand.  You sift through a few of them for a minute, grow bored, and put them back."

//Elevator Lobby Bulletin Board
"3_ElevatorBulletin" "This bulletin board is the main board for all announcements coming directly from President Marchand."

//Elevator Directory
"3_ElevatorDirectory" "The directory reads:<br><br>Next level:  Presidential Suite."


//MARCHAND's OFFICE

//Papers on Desk
"MarchandPapers" "The stack of papers on Marchand's desk reflect every piece of information that he and his staff have managed to dig up on key players in all of Marchand's dealings.   As you sift through the material, your brain starts to hurt, and you drop the papers back on the desk."

//Presidential Bookcase 1
"MarchandBooks1" "The books here all have to do with economic projections and financial policies.  This stuff makes the Sahara Desert feel like a water park."

//Presidential Bookcase 2
"MarchandBooks2" "The books here document local government issues, trade negotiation, and current law statutes.  This stuff is BORING!"

//Presidential Bookcase 3
"MarchandBooks3" "Several books on this shelf are biographical histories of presidents from across the globe.  At least this section has some pep."

//Waste Basket
"MarchandWasteBasket" "This waste basket has trash in it.  What did you expect?"

//Presidential Cabinets
"MarchandCabinets" "There are some seriously top secret files in here.  One file documents negotiations with the Soviets regarding the Warburg missiles and also some highly volatile correspondence with Kennedy.  Now THIS stuff is good.  What a gold mine!"

//Welded Beams
"RoofBeams" "The metal bolts holding this frame in place are loose.  Better stay off it, just in case."

//Vents
"RoofVents1" "You were up here earlier piping gas through the air system to knock people out.  You'd encounter less resistance that way."

//Rooftop Fountain Statue
"RoofFountainStatue" "Hm.  Looks hungry."

//More Vents
"RoofVents2" "You had problems with the vents on this side.  Maybe that's why you only managed to knock out a few people."
